[17592186065969 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065969 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c1c316a6-91b0-5ef2-a122-563a286b4d4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065970 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065970 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065970 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d7ffdc65-1540-5f47-9527-4662799e4709" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065971 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065971 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065971 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d070fd0-ee28-5aae-9b06-3677f53b9fd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065972 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\ln 5 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065972 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065972 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "43b27a57-5e6c-58c9-9aee-977fb1bb6433" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068457 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12450" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068457 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle 6t, 2t^2-1\\rangle,$ calculate $\\mathbf r (3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068457 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6eea01b2-bc2a-55a8-9bab-6789df00fc42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068457 #edb/ref 1074 "We substitute $t=3$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨6(3),\\,2(3)^{2}-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18,\\,17⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068458 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12451" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068458 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $\\left|\\mathbf r\\left(4\\right)\\right|$ given that $\\mathbf r(t)  = \\left\\langle 2-t, 2\\sqrt{t}, \\, t-1\\right\\rangle,$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068458 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86e423e7-db4b-5fdf-a285-bded3bd8161e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068458 #edb/ref 1074 "Evaluating the function at $t=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(4) & =⟨2-4,\\,2\\sqrt{4},\\,4-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(4)| & =\\sqrt{{(-2)}^{2}+{(4)}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068459 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12452" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068459 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the vector function $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle \\cos t, \\: \\sin t, \\: t \\right\\rangle$ at $t = \\pi.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ab3899d3-8838-57ad-8a17-b8ac2934c0f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068459 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate, we substitute $t = \\pi$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\pi ⟩=⟨-1,0,\\pi \\,⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $\\mathbf f (t)$ at $t = \\pi$ is $\\langle -1, 0, \\pi \\rangle.$\n\nWe can also express the answer using $\\mathbf i$-$\\mathbf j$-$\\mathbf k$ notation or square bracket notation, as follows:\n![](images/d9/d9ed4c8dcfbbc0fe7b4bf58e58197598221fc730613005a719252bf88c07d3f4.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068857 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387353 #edb/ref 17592